  "label": "Vocational Education",
  "description": "Vocational education refers to training programs that prepare individuals for specific trades or occupations, such as plumbing, electrical work, or automotive repair. It is often contrasted with academic education (like a 4-year college degree) and is promoted by advocates like Mike Rowe as a more practical and economically viable path to employment.",
